  "note": "Provenance of the two isolated environments used by tests/compatibility/runner.py. `binaries` are sha256 digests of the compiled extensions actually loaded by the child process, so a stale artifact is detectable; isolation itself is checked by path, because identical sources legitimately produce byte-identical artifacts in both trees. Regenerate with `python tests/compatibility/runner.py --write-manifest` after any rebuild; verify_manifest() reports every drift. Absolute paths and digests are machine-specific by design: they record what was actually measured, and a mismatch on another machine correctly means 'rebuild and regenerate', not 'ignore'.",
